# HabOS — Agent Onboarding & Development Guide

## 1. Project Mission & Identity
**HabOS** is a modular personal life operating system that unifies 24 life domains into a single connected platform. It replaces fragmented apps by linking tasks, software development projects, academic learning, physical fitness, personal finance, knowledge management, habits, and daily focus into a reactive ecosystem powered by an overarching **Life Score** and an AI assistant.

---

## 2. Primary Documentation References
Any AI agent working on this codebase MUST consult these primary documents before making architectural decisions or implementing features:
- **[System Architecture](file:///d:/HABos/docs/architecture.md)**: Full architecture specifications, clean architecture diagrams, database ER diagrams, and reactive event flows.
- **[Use Case Specifications](file:///d:/HABos/docs/usecases.md)**: Complete specifications for all 182 use cases across all 24 modules (UC-01 to UC-182).

---

## 3. Repository Anatomy

```
HABos/
├── client/                     # Flutter Mobile & Desktop Client Application
│   ├── assets/                 # Icons, images, illustrations
│   └── lib/
│       ├── app/                # App initialization, routing (GoRouter), theme configuration
│       ├── core/               # Shared networking (Dio), errors, constants, theme
│       ├── domain/             # Pure business rules (Entities, Repositories interfaces, UseCases)
│       ├── data/               # Models (DTOs), DataSources (Remote/Local), Repository implementations
│       ├── presentation/       # Riverpod Providers, Pages, and reusable Widgets
│       └── main.dart           # Entry point with ProviderScope
├── server/                     # Express.js + TypeScript REST API Backend
│   ├── prisma/
│   │   ├── schema.prisma       # Complete PostgreSQL database schema
│   │   └── seed.ts             # Initial database seed script (TypeScript)
│   ├── tsconfig.json           # TypeScript configuration
│   └── src/
│       ├── server.ts           # HTTP listener startup
│       ├── app.ts              # Express app configuration & route registry
│       ├── config/             # Environment, database, and JWT configuration
│       ├── middleware/         # Auth, validation, rate limiting, error handling
│       ├── modules/            # 24 Domain-driven backend TypeScript modules
│       ├── jobs/               # Cron jobs (midnight streak validation, reminder queue)
│       └── utils/              # Calculation engines (LifeScore, streaks, date utils)
├── docs/                       # Architecture, use cases, API, and database specs
├── docker-compose.yml          # PostgreSQL & Node.js orchestration
└── README.md                   # Project overview
```

