## 6. How to Implement a New Feature (Agent Recipe)

When an agent is assigned to implement a use case (e.g., `UC-XX`):

```mermaid
graph TD
    Step1["1. Consult docs/usecases.md for requirements, preconditions, and flows"]
    Step2["2. Check & update server/prisma/schema.prisma if DB models/fields needed"]
    Step3["3. Run prisma generate & prisma migrate dev"]
    Step4["4. Implement Backend: validation.js -> service.js -> controller.js -> routes.js"]
    Step5["5. Register module route in server/src/app.js"]
    Step6["6. Implement Frontend: domain/ (Entity/UseCase) -> data/ (Model/DataSource/Repo)"]
    Step7["7. Implement Frontend: presentation/ (Riverpod Provider & Screen Widgets)"]
    Step8["8. Verify inter-module hooks (Life Score / Dashboard updates)"]

    Step1 --> Step2 --> Step3 --> Step4 --> Step5 --> Step6 --> Step7 --> Step8
```

---

## 7. Essential Development Commands

### Backend Commands (run in `/server`):
```bash
# Start development server with live reload
npm run dev

# Generate Prisma Client after schema changes
npm run prisma:generate

# Run database migrations
npm run prisma:migrate

# Seed the database
npm run prisma:seed

# Run backend tests
npm test
```

### Frontend Commands (run in `/client`):
```bash
# Install Flutter dependencies
flutter pub get

# Run Flutter application
flutter run

# Run Flutter unit and widget tests
flutter test

# Analyze code quality
flutter analyze
```

### Full Stack Docker Environment (run in root `/`):
```bash
# Start PostgreSQL & API backend in containers
docker compose up -d

# View container logs
docker compose logs -f
```
